        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): bound batch create error body read",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`response.text()` in the Gemini batch create non-404 error path embeds the\nfull response body in the Error message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced raw `response.text()` + `throw Error` with `createProviderHttpError`\nfor non-404 errors. Preserves 404 diagnostic message. Pattern from #102953.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** unbounded body in error message\n**After:** bounded + redacted via `createProviderHttpError`\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Targeted path proof (Gemini batch-create via createProviderHttpError)\n\nReal HTTP 400 with sensitive Google API error body → `createProviderHttpError(response, \"gemini.batch-create\")`:\n\n```\n=== #103472 Proof: createProviderHttpError on Gemini batch-create path ===\nError name ProviderHttpError: PASS\nStatus 400: PASS\nLabel \"gemini.batch-create\": PASS\nStatus in message: PASS\nAPI_KEY_INVALID not in message: PASS\nRaw JSON not in message: PASS\nService domain not in message: PASS\nStructured code INVALID_ARGUMENT: PASS\nError body bounded: PASS\n\nMessage: gemini.batch-create (400): The API key included in the request is invalid. [code=INVALID_ARGUMENT]\nCode: INVALID_ARGUMENT\nStatus: 400\n\nOverall: ALL PASS\n```\n\n### Tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google/embedding-batch.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n```\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nextensions/google/embedding-batch.ts | 3 +-- (createProviderHttpError)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
